# Bee Crypto Worker Project Rules

## Documentation Map
Always consult the documentation in `doc/` before modifying architectural, database, or algorithmic components:
- `doc/01_TECHNICAL_SPECIFICATION.md` — SaaS monetization, business model, architecture.
- `doc/02_STRATEGY_AND_BACKTESTS.md` — Market-neutral alpha math, 4 pairs basket, backtests.
- `doc/03_DATABASE_SCHEMA.sql` — Supabase PostgreSQL schema, RLS, Realtime.
- `doc/04_WORKER_ENGINE_SPECIFICATION.md` — Railway daemon, CCXT integration, encryption.
- `doc/05_FRONTEND_AND_UI_SPECIFICATION.md` — UI/UX Next.js specifications.
- `doc/06_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP_AND_AGENTS_GUIDE.md` — Implementation roadmap.
- `AGENTS.md` — Full AI Agent Handbook.

## Language and UI Rules
- Always reply to the user in **Russian** (Русский).
- All code interface text, labels, buttons, console logs, and errors must be in **English only**.

## Strategy & Risk Constraints
- Basket consists of 4 pairs: `ZEC/AVAX`, `ENA/SUI`, `SOL/ADA`, `BNB/ETH`.
- Entry condition: `Ratio > EMA10` on 4h timeframe.
- Margin split: 25% of available free margin per pair.
- Leverage: 7.0x.
- Take Profit: +5.0% on net pair.
- Stop Loss: -1.5% on net pair.
- Trend Flip: immediate market exit if ratio drops below EMA10.

## Security Rules
- API keys MUST be encrypted with AES-256-GCM before database storage (`worker/src/security/encryption.ts`).
- NEVER store unencrypted keys or keys with withdrawal permissions enabled.
- All critical actions (bot toggle, delete keys, logout) require confirmation modals (`ConfirmModal.tsx`).
- Emergency liquidation requires typing `CLOSE` in `PanicCloseModal.tsx`.
- Overdue invoice policy: **Variant A (Safe Freeze)** — block new trades, continue managing open positions until TP/SL.

## Database & Tech Stack
- Supabase Project ID: `uxsbjkymrqrmlcshizns` (PostgreSQL with RLS on all tables).
- Next.js 15 (App Router) in `web/` (`distDir` separates `.next-dev` and `.next`).
- When checking TypeScript in `web/`, use `npx tsc --noEmit`. NEVER run `npm run build` solely for type checks while the user is testing the dev server.
- Railway Worker Daemon in `worker/` (Static Egress IP `54.198.120.45`).
